Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA
bundle. q2-qobuz runs from the card's .qobuz folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's patch/addon.c):
Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page and keeps the Q2 awake while it
downloads. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.qobuz, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-qobuz-vX.Y-SHA.zip
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .qobuz/run: q2-qobuz copied to /tmp and run there at nice 10 in a
               restart loop
  q2app        name=Qobuz, search=Search Qobuz, qr=0 (the QR code opens from a row)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               Streaming's row icon, 52 px and 40 px: a Q in white on near-black
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.qobuz/run when Streaming's Qobuz row is pressed and it isn't running;
the launcher copies q2-qobuz and itself to /tmp, restarts it after a failure (5 s, doubling to a
minute) and leaves the loop's pid in /tmp/q2-qobuz. An exit of 0 (turned off, or idle 15 minutes with
nothing to download) ends it; a TERM stops it, keeping a download under way to resume.

  /tmp/q2-qobuz.state        addr, pin, qr, qrsize, note, hold, version (as q2-podcasts')
  /tmp/q2-qobuz.sock         datagrams: q quits
  /tmp/q2-qobuz.browse.sock  Q2SPOT/1 for the Q2's page (cmd/q2-qobuz/device.go lists the levels)
  port 8300                  the phone page (the next free one if taken)
  /mnt/data/q2-qobuz/        the sign-in, in the Q2's own storage (-private)

Qobuz
-----

The API is the web player's, www.qobuz.com/api.json/0.2, with X-App-Id and X-User-Auth-Token. The app
id, the sign-in key and the per-region secrets are read from the web player's script
(play.qobuz.com/login names it), kept in .qobuz/creds.json and read again once a run and when a
request is refused, the script only when it has changed (internal/qobuz/creds.go). The secret that
signs this account's file requests is found by trying each on the newest liked song Qobuz streams
(an answer without a file still takes the signature), and kept with the sign-in.

Sign-in: the phone page sends the phone to www.qobuz.com/signin/oauth with this app id and a return
address on the Q2, /signin/<nonce> (one use, 15 minutes: Qobuz's redirect brings no cookie). Qobuz
returns with code_autorisation, which oauth/callback trades, with the script's private key, for the
account's token. A 401 later forgets the token and asks for a new sign-in; the lists and downloads
stay.

Files: track/getFileUrl (format_id 6, 7 or 27, intent stream, request_ts, request_sig the MD5 of
"trackgetFileUrl", the arguments in name order, the time and the secret) gives a short-lived
address of a plain FLAC, at the best format the track has up to the one asked. Its files carry no
tags: the downloader reads its metadata blocks, writes a new start (STREAMINFO and SEEKTABLE kept,
Vorbis comments from the catalogue, the album's 600 px cover, 4 KB of padding), then the frames as
they come. partial/<id>.json keeps where the two starts end, so a break resumes with a Range (a .part
already whole starts again). A track Qobuz answers without a file fails at once. A track another
folder has is copied, not downloaded. After each download the cache is trimmed, oldest first, to
Download Space.

Library: favorite/getUserFavorites (albums, tracks, artists) and playlist/getUserPlaylists, read 500
at a time to their totals, kept in .qobuz/lists and read again after 30 minutes; album/get,
playlist/get (extra=tracks, paged), artist/get (extra=albums) and catalog/search when opened.
